# text = this view of marner 's personality was not without another ground than his pale face and unexampled eyes ; for jem rodney , the mole-catcher , averred that one evening as he was returning homeward , he saw silas marner leaning against a stile with a heavy bag on his back , instead of resting the bag on the stile as a man in his senses would have done ; and that , on coming up to him , he saw that marner 's eyes were set like a dead man 's , and he spoke to him , and shook him , and his limbs were stiff , and his hands clutched the bag as if they 'd been made of iron ; but just as he had made up his mind that the weaver was dead , he came all right again , like , as you might say , in the winking of an eye , and said " good-night " , and walked off .
